{"schema":1,"id":"Development.AutomorphicArithmetic.AutomorphicVarieties.NumberFieldTowers.ExistsDescends:26:9","name":"UpperTheory.V.Tower.step0","kind":"theorem","file":"Development/AutomorphicArithmetic/AutomorphicVarieties/NumberFieldTowers/ExistsDescends.lean","lines":[26,46],"atlasRow":412270,"chapter":"1.5992","archiveCommit":"40e56bab026552e089d7afcfeff08d2defb9c005","provenance":{"fileSha256":"ad5198ddc985ff0ef9c7f4f15962c2a9584836b35f8c923027e9ea3bdd8c411d","commandSha256":"17c4c66b71c8211a3e122a0bda259b8de82312da02f4e6c4a687163ffbc42298"},"source":["theorem step0 (hμ : HasMuQ l L₀) {γ : G L₀ Ω} (hγ : IsGen l ⊤ γ) {e : ℤ} (he : e ≠ 0) (m : ℕ) (L₁ : Type) [Field L₁]","    [NumberField L₁] [Algebra L₀ L₁] (hL : IsLayer l m L₀ L₁) :","    shaInv L₁ l e = cokerLen (xTw l l (⊤ : Subgroup (G L₀ Ω)) e γ ^ l ^ m - 1) := by","  haveI : IsAlgClosed Ω := IsAlgClosure.isAlgClosed L₀","  haveI : FiniteDimensional L₀ L₁ := Module.Finite.of_restrictScalars_finite ℚ L₀ L₁","  let j : L₁ →ₐ[L₀] Ω := IsAlgClosed.lift","  letI : Algebra L₁ Ω := j.toRingHom.toAlgebra","  haveI : IsScalarTower L₀ L₁ Ω := IsScalarTower.of_algebraMap_eq fun x => (j.commutes x).symm","  haveI : Algebra.IsAlgebraic L₀ Ω := IsAlgClosure.isAlgebraic","  haveI : IsAlgClosure L₁ Ω := ⟨inferInstance, Algebra.IsAlgebraic.tower_top (K := L₀) L₁⟩","  obtain ⟨D⟩ := Formalism.GaloisCohomology.ldataExists L₁ Ω l","  have hμ₁ : HasMuQ l L₁ := by","    obtain ⟨ζ, hζ⟩ := hμ","    exact ⟨_, hζ.map_of_injective (algebraMap L₀ L₁).injective⟩","  have hU := (layerUniq L₀ Ω l hμ).2.1 m L₁ hL","  obtain ⟨Φ, -⟩ := desc L₀ L₁ Ω l D e ⊤ he ((muQ L₁ Ω l).2.2.2.1 hμ₁).2 (by rw [hU, cycU_levU])","  have hg := ((layerGen L₀ Ω l hμ).2 γ hγ).2.2 m","  rw [← hU] at hg","  rw [← shaLen_eq_shaInv D, shaLen, Φ.length_eq, (shaDGen L₀ Ω l l ⊤ _ e _ isClosed_univ le_top hg).2, ← map_pow]","  exact (cokerDual l _ _ _ fun x φ => by","    rw [LinearMap.sub_apply, LinearMap.sub_apply, LinearMap.sub_apply, map_sub, xTw_apply_apply]; rfl).symm"],"statementLines":[26,28],"proofLines":[28,46],"assume":["Assume `HasMuQ l L₀` (hμ).","Assume `IsGen l ⊤ γ` (hγ).","Assume `e ≠ 0` (he).","Assume `IsLayer l m L₀ L₁` (hL)."],"show":"Let the base number field satisfy the required ℓ-power roots-of-unity hypothesis. Let γ be a Galois element whose character value topologically generates the cyclotomic image, let e be a nonzero integer twist, and let L₁ be a field at layer m. The arithmetic length on L₁ equals the cokernel length of Tₑ(γ)^(ℓᵐ)−I, where Tₑ(γ) denotes the action on the twisted dual module at twist e.","strategy":"Embed the layer in the given algebraic closure and identify its fixing subgroup. Descent and the generator of its cyclotomic image express the arithmetic length as a kernel length. The dual cokernel formula yields the claimed equality.","steps":[{"id":"g-29-3","number":"⟨1⟩1","kind":"have","claim":"The chosen algebraic closure Ω of L₀ is algebraically closed, so it can receive an embedding of the algebraic extension L₁/L₀.","lines":[29,29],"headLines":[29,29],"snippet":"  haveI : IsAlgClosed Ω := IsAlgClosure.isAlgClosed L₀","uses":[],"refs":[],"typedFact":"IsAlgClosed Ω","secondRead":true,"children":[]},{"id":"g-30-3","number":"⟨1⟩2","kind":"have","claim":"The extension L₁/L₀ is finite dimensional because L₁ has finite dimension over ℚ and ℚ ⊆ L₀ ⊆ L₁.","lines":[30,30],"headLines":[30,30],"snippet":"  haveI : FiniteDimensional L₀ L₁ := Module.Finite.of_restrictScalars_finite ℚ L₀ L₁","uses":[],"refs":[],"typedFact":"FiniteDimensional L₀ L₁","secondRead":true,"children":[]},{"id":"g-31-3","number":"⟨1⟩3","kind":"setup","claim":"Choose an L₀-embedding j of the finite algebraic extension L₁ into the algebraically closed field Ω. Use j to make Ω an extension of L₁.","lines":[31,32],"headLines":[31,32],"snippet":"  let j : L₁ →ₐ[L₀] Ω := IsAlgClosed.lift\n  letI : Algebra L₁ Ω := j.toRingHom.toAlgebra","uses":[],"refs":[],"typedFact":null,"secondRead":true,"children":[]},{"id":"g-33-3","number":"⟨1⟩4","kind":"have","claim":"For x ∈ L₀, j sends the image of x in L₁ to the given image of x in Ω. Thus the embeddings L₀ → L₁ → Ω form a compatible tower.","lines":[33,33],"headLines":[33,33],"snippet":"  haveI : IsScalarTower L₀ L₁ Ω := IsScalarTower.of_algebraMap_eq fun x => (j.commutes x).symm","uses":[],"refs":[],"typedFact":"IsScalarTower L₀ L₁ Ω","secondRead":true,"children":[]},{"id":"g-34-3","number":"⟨1⟩5","kind":"have","claim":"Every element of Ω is algebraic over L₀ because Ω is its algebraic closure.","lines":[34,34],"headLines":[34,34],"snippet":"  haveI : Algebra.IsAlgebraic L₀ Ω := IsAlgClosure.isAlgebraic","uses":[],"refs":[],"typedFact":"Algebra.IsAlgebraic L₀ Ω","secondRead":true,"children":[]},{"id":"g-35-3","number":"⟨1⟩6","kind":"have","claim":"The same Ω is an algebraic closure of L₁. It is algebraically closed and algebraicity over L₀ implies algebraicity over its embedded overfield L₁.","lines":[35,35],"headLines":[35,35],"snippet":"  haveI : IsAlgClosure L₁ Ω := ⟨inferInstance, Algebra.IsAlgebraic.tower_top (K := L₀) L₁⟩","uses":[],"refs":[],"typedFact":"IsAlgClosure L₁ Ω","secondRead":true,"children":[]},{"id":"g-36-3","number":"⟨1⟩7","kind":"have","claim":"Choose a local datum D for L₁ in Ω. It consists of the primes of L₁ above ℓ, a prolongation of each valuation to Ω, and a character χ on the Galois quotient unramified outside these primes whose pullback is the cyclotomic character. The local maps define Sha(D,e) with coefficients ℚℓ/ℤℓ acted on through χ^(−e).","lines":[36,36],"headLines":[36,36],"snippet":"  obtain ⟨D⟩ := Formalism.GaloisCohomology.ldataExists L₁ Ω l","uses":[{"id":"Formalism.GaloisCohomology.GaloisCohomologyProofs.LdataNonempty:48:9","name":"Formalism.GaloisCohomology.ldataExists","kind":"theorem","file":"Formalism/GaloisCohomology/GaloisCohomologyProofs/LdataNonempty.lean","lines":[48,50],"atlasRow":580818,"owner":"1.10567"}],"refs":[],"typedFact":null,"secondRead":true,"children":[]},{"id":"g-37-3","number":"⟨1⟩8","kind":"have","claim":"A primitive root ζ in L₀ of order 4 at ℓ = 2 or of order ℓ at odd ℓ retains that exact order under the injective field map L₀ → L₁. Hence L₁ satisfies the required roots-of-unity hypothesis.","lines":[37,39],"headLines":[37,39],"snippet":"  have hμ₁ : HasMuQ l L₁ := by\n    obtain ⟨ζ, hζ⟩ := hμ\n    exact ⟨_, hζ.map_of_injective (algebraMap L₀ L₁).injective⟩","uses":[{"id":"Development.AutomorphicArithmetic.AutomorphicVarieties.GeneratorCountTuples.LemmaK:9:5","name":"UpperTheory.V.HasMuQ","kind":"def","file":"Development/AutomorphicArithmetic/AutomorphicVarieties/GeneratorCountTuples/LemmaK.lean","lines":[9,9],"atlasRow":null,"owner":"1.6325"}],"refs":[],"typedFact":"HasMuQ l L₁","secondRead":true,"children":[]},{"id":"g-40-3","number":"⟨1⟩9","kind":"have","claim":"Write H = Gal(Ω/j(L₁)) and let c₀ be the greatest c for which L₀ contains a primitive root of order ℓᶜ. Uniqueness of the cyclotomic layer of degree ℓᵐ gives H = {σ ∈ Gal(Ω/L₀) | κ(σ) ≡ 1 modulo ℓ^(c₀+m)}.","lines":[40,40],"headLines":[40,40],"snippet":"  have hU := (layerUniq L₀ Ω l hμ).2.1 m L₁ hL","uses":[{"id":"Development.AutomorphicArithmetic.AutomorphicVarieties.NumberFieldTowers.LayerUniq:25:9","name":"UpperTheory.V.Tower.layerUniq","kind":"theorem","file":"Development/AutomorphicArithmetic/AutomorphicVarieties/NumberFieldTowers/LayerUniq.lean","lines":[25,43],"atlasRow":412291,"owner":"1.5992"}],"refs":[],"typedFact":null,"secondRead":true,"children":[]},{"id":"g-41-3","number":"⟨1⟩10","kind":"rewrite","claim":"Descent requires either ℓ ≠ 2 or trivial action of Gal(Ω/L₁) on the fourth roots of unity. At ℓ = 2 the primitive fourth root in L₁ gives this trivial action. The congruence defining H gives H ∩ ker κ = ker κ. Since e ≠ 0, descent supplies an ℤℓ-linear isomorphism Φ from Sha(D,e) to the H-invariants in D∞, the base descent character module on ker κ at parameter ℓ. Its action Dₑ is conjugation on characters twisted by κ^(−e).","lines":[41,41],"headLines":[41,41],"snippet":"  obtain ⟨Φ, -⟩ := desc L₀ L₁ Ω l D e ⊤ he ((muQ L₁ Ω l).2.2.2.1 hμ₁).2 (by rw [hU, cycU_levU])","uses":[{"id":"Development.AutomorphicArithmetic.AutomorphicVarieties.GaloisLibrary.SelmerTransport.ConjStableShaFam:209:9","name":"UpperTheory.V.Base.cycU_levU","kind":"theorem","file":"Development/AutomorphicArithmetic/AutomorphicVarieties/GaloisLibrary/SelmerTransport/ConjStableShaFam.lean","lines":[209,210],"atlasRow":393843,"owner":"1.6302"},{"id":"Development.AutomorphicArithmetic.AutomorphicVarieties.NumberFieldTowers.CycMemPrincIff:81:9","name":"UpperTheory.V.Tower.muQ","kind":"theorem","file":"Development/AutomorphicArithmetic/AutomorphicVarieties/NumberFieldTowers/CycMemPrincIff.lean","lines":[81,104],"atlasRow":412261,"owner":"1.6879"},{"id":"Development.AutomorphicArithmetic.AutomorphicVarieties.NumberFieldTowers.Imports:10:9","name":"UpperTheory.V.Tower.desc","kind":"theorem","file":"Development/AutomorphicArithmetic/AutomorphicVarieties/NumberFieldTowers/Imports.lean","lines":[10,147],"atlasRow":412288,"owner":"1.6879"}],"refs":["g-37-3"],"typedFact":null,"secondRead":true,"children":[]},{"id":"g-42-3","number":"⟨1⟩11","kind":"rewrite","claim":"Put η = γ^(ℓᵐ). As κ(γ) generates the base cyclotomic image topologically, the layer generator theorem gives η in the canonical mth layer subgroup with character generating its image. By the identification of that subgroup with H, η ∈ H and κ(H) ⊆ closure⟨κ(η)⟩.","lines":[42,43],"headLines":[42,43],"snippet":"  have hg := ((layerGen L₀ Ω l hμ).2 γ hγ).2.2 m\n  rw [← hU] at hg","uses":[{"id":"Development.AutomorphicArithmetic.AutomorphicVarieties.NumberFieldTowers.LayerGen:10:9","name":"UpperTheory.V.Tower.layerGen","kind":"theorem","file":"Development/AutomorphicArithmetic/AutomorphicVarieties/NumberFieldTowers/LayerGen.lean","lines":[10,39],"atlasRow":412289,"owner":"1.5992"}],"refs":[],"typedFact":null,"secondRead":true,"children":[]},{"id":"g-44-3","number":"⟨1⟩12","kind":"rewrite","claim":"The comparison with Sha(D,e) and the isomorphism Φ give shaInv(L₁,ℓ,e) as the length of the H-invariants in D∞. Since η is a cyclotomic generator for H, this submodule equals ker(Dₑ(η⁻¹)−I). On the character dual X∞ = Homℤℓ(D∞,ℚℓ/ℤℓ), the representation law yields Xₑ(γ)^(ℓᵐ) = Xₑ(η).","lines":[44,44],"headLines":[44,44],"snippet":"  rw [← shaLen_eq_shaInv D, shaLen, Φ.length_eq, (shaDGen L₀ Ω l l ⊤ _ e _ isClosed_univ le_top hg).2, ← map_pow]","uses":[{"id":"Development.AutomorphicArithmetic.AutomorphicVarieties.GaloisLibrary.GaloisCohomologyLength.ShaLenEqShaInv:58:9","name":"UpperTheory.V.LDataCardLeFinrank.shaLen_eq_shaInv","kind":"theorem","file":"Development/AutomorphicArithmetic/AutomorphicVarieties/GaloisLibrary/GaloisCohomologyLength/ShaLenEqShaInv.lean","lines":[58,60],"atlasRow":393501,"owner":"1.6283"},{"id":"Development.AutomorphicArithmetic.AutomorphicVarieties.NumberFieldTowers.ShaDGen:9:9","name":"UpperTheory.V.Tower.shaDGen","kind":"theorem","file":"Development/AutomorphicArithmetic/AutomorphicVarieties/NumberFieldTowers/ShaDGen.lean","lines":[9,59],"atlasRow":412311,"owner":"1.6879"},{"id":"Formalism.GaloisCohomology.Statement:78:5","name":"Formalism.GaloisCohomology.shaLen","kind":"def","file":"Formalism/GaloisCohomology/Statement.lean","lines":[78,78],"atlasRow":null,"owner":"1.10568"}],"refs":[],"typedFact":null,"secondRead":true,"children":[]},{"id":"g-45-3","number":"⟨1⟩13","kind":"rewrite","claim":"For every x ∈ X∞ and φ ∈ D∞, evaluation gives ((Xₑ(η)−I)x)(φ) = x(Dₑ(η⁻¹)φ)−x(φ) = x((Dₑ(η⁻¹)−I)φ). The inverse in the pairing gives κ(η⁻¹)^(−e) = κ(η)^e, the twist on X∞. The dual cokernel formula therefore identifies the kernel length on D∞ with the cokernel length of Xₑ(γ)^(ℓᵐ)−I on X∞.","lines":[45,46],"headLines":[45,46],"snippet":"  exact (cokerDual l _ _ _ fun x φ => by\n    rw [LinearMap.sub_apply, LinearMap.sub_apply, LinearMap.sub_apply, map_sub, xTw_apply_apply]; rfl).symm","uses":[{"id":"Development.AutomorphicArithmetic.AutomorphicVarieties.NumberFieldTowers.CokerDual:8:9","name":"UpperTheory.V.Tower.cokerDual","kind":"theorem","file":"Development/AutomorphicArithmetic/AutomorphicVarieties/NumberFieldTowers/CokerDual.lean","lines":[8,19],"atlasRow":412256,"owner":"1.5992"},{"id":"Development.AutomorphicArithmetic.AutomorphicVarieties.NumberFieldTowers.XTwApplyApply:66:9","name":"UpperTheory.V.Tower.xTw_apply_apply","kind":"theorem","file":"Development/AutomorphicArithmetic/AutomorphicVarieties/NumberFieldTowers/XTwApplyApply.lean","lines":[66,69],"atlasRow":412317,"owner":"1.6879"}],"refs":[],"typedFact":null,"secondRead":true,"children":[]}],"uses":[{"id":"Development.AutomorphicArithmetic.AutomorphicVarieties.AdditiveValuationNorms.CokLenLeOfRangeLe:16:5","name":"UpperTheory.V.PropA.IsLevel","kind":"def","file":"Development/AutomorphicArithmetic/AutomorphicVarieties/AdditiveValuationNorms/CokLenLeOfRangeLe.lean","lines":[16,16],"atlasRow":null,"owner":"1.5992"},{"id":"Development.AutomorphicArithmetic.AutomorphicVarieties.GaloisLibrary.GaloisCohomologyLength.LevelInertiaLeLevelDec:70:5","name":"UpperTheory.V.LDataCardLeFinrank.shaInv","kind":"def","file":"Development/AutomorphicArithmetic/AutomorphicVarieties/GaloisLibrary/GaloisCohomologyLength/LevelInertiaLeLevelDec.lean","lines":[70,71],"atlasRow":null,"owner":"1.6283"},{"id":"Development.AutomorphicArithmetic.AutomorphicVarieties.GaloisLibrary.KummerTheory.Mk0IdMapCongr:186:8","name":"UpperTheory.V.Kum.Un","kind":"abbrev","file":"Development/AutomorphicArithmetic/AutomorphicVarieties/GaloisLibrary/KummerTheory/Mk0IdMapCongr.lean","lines":[186,186],"atlasRow":null,"owner":"1.6292"},{"id":"Development.AutomorphicArithmetic.AutomorphicVarieties.GaloisLibrary.KummerTheory.Mk0IdMapCongr:191:5","name":"UpperTheory.V.Kum.Procyc","kind":"def","file":"Development/AutomorphicArithmetic/AutomorphicVarieties/GaloisLibrary/KummerTheory/Mk0IdMapCongr.lean","lines":[191,191],"atlasRow":null,"owner":"1.6292"},{"id":"Development.AutomorphicArithmetic.AutomorphicVarieties.GaloisLibrary.KummerTheory.Mk0IdMapCongr:195:8","name":"UpperTheory.V.Kum.Dinf","kind":"abbrev","file":"Development/AutomorphicArithmetic/AutomorphicVarieties/GaloisLibrary/KummerTheory/Mk0IdMapCongr.lean","lines":[195,195],"atlasRow":null,"owner":"1.6292"},{"id":"Development.AutomorphicArithmetic.AutomorphicVarieties.GaloisLibrary.KummerTheory.Mk0IdMapCongr:197:8","name":"UpperTheory.V.Kum.Xinf","kind":"abbrev","file":"Development/AutomorphicArithmetic/AutomorphicVarieties/GaloisLibrary/KummerTheory/Mk0IdMapCongr.lean","lines":[197,197],"atlasRow":null,"owner":"1.6292"},{"id":"Development.AutomorphicArithmetic.AutomorphicVarieties.GaloisLibrary.SelmerTransport.ConjStableShaFam:43:5","name":"UpperTheory.V.Base.galOf","kind":"def","file":"Development/AutomorphicArithmetic/AutomorphicVarieties/GaloisLibrary/SelmerTransport/ConjStableShaFam.lean","lines":[43,47],"atlasRow":null,"owner":"1.6302"},{"id":"Development.AutomorphicArithmetic.AutomorphicVarieties.GaloisLibrary.SelmerTransport.ConjStableShaFam:187:5","name":"UpperTheory.V.Base.levU","kind":"def","file":"Development/AutomorphicArithmetic/AutomorphicVarieties/GaloisLibrary/SelmerTransport/ConjStableShaFam.lean","lines":[187,187],"atlasRow":null,"owner":"1.6302"},{"id":"Development.AutomorphicArithmetic.AutomorphicVarieties.GaloisLibrary.SelmerTransport.ConjStableShaFam:189:5","name":"UpperTheory.V.Base.cycU","kind":"def","file":"Development/AutomorphicArithmetic/AutomorphicVarieties/GaloisLibrary/SelmerTransport/ConjStableShaFam.lean","lines":[189,189],"atlasRow":null,"owner":"1.6302"},{"id":"Development.AutomorphicArithmetic.AutomorphicVarieties.GaloisLibrary.SelmerTransport.ConjStableShaFam:193:5","name":"UpperTheory.V.Base.qExp","kind":"def","file":"Development/AutomorphicArithmetic/AutomorphicVarieties/GaloisLibrary/SelmerTransport/ConjStableShaFam.lean","lines":[193,193],"atlasRow":null,"owner":"1.6302"},{"id":"Development.AutomorphicArithmetic.AutomorphicVarieties.NumberFieldTowers.IdealNormClassCongr:99:5","name":"UpperTheory.V.Tower.IsDesc","kind":"def","file":"Development/AutomorphicArithmetic/AutomorphicVarieties/NumberFieldTowers/IdealNormClassCongr.lean","lines":[99,101],"atlasRow":null,"owner":"1.6879"},{"id":"Development.AutomorphicArithmetic.AutomorphicVarieties.NumberFieldTowers.XTwApplyApply:24:5","name":"UpperTheory.V.Tower.cokerLen","kind":"def","file":"Development/AutomorphicArithmetic/AutomorphicVarieties/NumberFieldTowers/XTwApplyApply.lean","lines":[24,25],"atlasRow":null,"owner":"1.6879"},{"id":"Development.AutomorphicArithmetic.AutomorphicVarieties.NumberFieldTowers.XTwApplyApply:36:5","name":"UpperTheory.V.Tower.IsGen","kind":"def","file":"Development/AutomorphicArithmetic/AutomorphicVarieties/NumberFieldTowers/XTwApplyApply.lean","lines":[36,37],"atlasRow":null,"owner":"1.6879"},{"id":"Development.AutomorphicArithmetic.AutomorphicVarieties.NumberFieldTowers.XTwApplyApply:56:5","name":"UpperTheory.V.Tower.dTw","kind":"def","file":"Development/AutomorphicArithmetic/AutomorphicVarieties/NumberFieldTowers/XTwApplyApply.lean","lines":[56,56],"atlasRow":null,"owner":"1.6879"},{"id":"Development.AutomorphicArithmetic.AutomorphicVarieties.NumberFieldTowers.XTwApplyApply:58:5","name":"UpperTheory.V.Tower.xTw","kind":"def","file":"Development/AutomorphicArithmetic/AutomorphicVarieties/NumberFieldTowers/XTwApplyApply.lean","lines":[58,58],"atlasRow":null,"owner":"1.6879"},{"id":"Development.AutomorphicArithmetic.AutomorphicVarieties.NumberFieldTowers.XTwApplyApply:73:8","name":"UpperTheory.V.Tower.ShaD","kind":"abbrev","file":"Development/AutomorphicArithmetic/AutomorphicVarieties/NumberFieldTowers/XTwApplyApply.lean","lines":[73,74],"atlasRow":null,"owner":"1.6879"},{"id":"Development.AutomorphicArithmetic.AutomorphicVarieties.NumberFieldTowers.XTwApplyApply:104:5","name":"UpperTheory.V.Tower.cZero","kind":"def","file":"Development/AutomorphicArithmetic/AutomorphicVarieties/NumberFieldTowers/XTwApplyApply.lean","lines":[104,104],"atlasRow":null,"owner":"